  "sections": {
    "BASICS": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [],
      "subsections": {
        "OVERVIEW": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "canonical_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Inflammation of the lungs caused by inhalation of oral ingesta, regurgitated material, and vomitus with subsequent pulmonary dysfunction; develops when laryngeal reflexes function improperly or are",
              "pdf_page": 1167,
              "printed_page": 1085,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "overwhelmed.",
              "pdf_page": 1167,
              "printed_page": 1085,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Pulmonary dysfunction— caused by (1) direct obstruction of small airways and indirect obstruction from bronchospasm and production of mucus and exudate; (2) aspiration of gastric acid— damages respiratory epithelium; can cause bronchospasm and acute lung injury/acute respiratory distress syndrome (ALI/ARDS); (3) bacterial pneumonia—bacteria in aspirated material can initiate an immediate infection; or later infections occur secondary to lung damage.",
              "pdf_page": 1167,
              "printed_page": 1085,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "DEFINITION": {
          "present": false,
          "status": "missing",
          "source_heading": null,
          "canonical_heading": "DEFINITION",
          "content_blocks": []
        },
